  "identifier": "kernR",
  "description": "Kernel-based hypothesis tests for causal inference and distributional treatment effects. Implements backdoor-adjusted HSIC (bd-HSIC) for testing causal association, and doubly robust kernel statistics (DR-DATE, DR-DETT) for testing distributional treatment effects beyond mean shifts. Supports binary, continuous, and mixed treatments, hierarchical/nested data structures, and scales to larger datasets via Nystrom approximation and random Fourier features.",
  "name": "kernR: Kernel-Based Causal Distributional Testing",
